WEBVTT

00:00:00.319 --> 00:00:01.880
How do we predict tomorrow's inventory

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:04.180
risk? Does the ontology agent just

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:07.000
guess? The source material draws a

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.300
very sharp, deliberate line here regarding

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.960
predictive analytics. Forecasting is

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:14.140
treated as a separate, highly rigorous

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:16.379
analytical discipline. It's not just

00:00:16.379 --> 00:00:17.140
a chat function.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.220
You don't just ask the generative

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:21.160
AI chat to guess what sales

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:22.600
will look like next week based

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.180
on vibes or its training data.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:27.900
Forecasting is explicitly handled via

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:29.200
Fabric data science.

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:31.080
So we are talking about actual

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:32.740
machine learning engineers, building

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:34.739
notebooks, running experiments, and

00:00:34.739 --> 00:00:36.059
scoring dedicated models.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:38.960
Yes. A data scientist defines the

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:41.199
target variable, sets the time horizon,

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:43.500
selects the inputs, and chooses the

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.600
statistical methodology inside a data

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:46.339
science notebook.
